  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Find $g(1)$ given that $g(t)$ is a continuous vector-valued function and $u(t)$ is continuous real-valued function for which $u(1)=5$ and \n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to 1}[u(t)g(t)]=\u27e85,-10,20\u27e9\\,.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the scalar function multiple rule for limits, and the fact that both functions are continuous, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}[u(t)g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 1}u(t)\\cdot {lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) \\\\  & =u(1)g(1) \\\\  & =5g(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, we are told that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to 1}[u(t)g(t)]=\u27e85,-10,20\u27e9\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following equation which we can solve for $g(1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}[u(t)g(t)] & =\u27e85,-10,20\u27e9 \\\\ 5g(1) & =\u27e85,-10,2\u27e9 \\\\ g(1) & =\\frac{1}{5}\u27e85,-10,20\u27e9 \\\\ g(1) & =\u27e81,-2,4\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
